  "releaseNotes": "This release introduces significant improvements to performance, stability, and adherence to modern development practices. Critical code paths have been optimized to use CallContext.CurrentOrDefault, preventing memory leaks in client applications. A new CurrentOrDefault property has been added to CallContext, enabling safe access to the current context without implicitly creating one, improving control over uninitialized contexts.\n\nThe TraceId property has been removed from CallContext, with applications now expected to rely on ASP.NET Core’s Activity.Current.TraceId and its support for the W3C traceparent header standard. This simplifies trace management while aligning with modern frameworks and best practices. Additionally, automatic instantiation of traceId on the first usage of CallContext.Current has been removed, requiring explicit initialization via the Initialize method to reduce the risk of improper usage and memory leaks. Fixes were also applied to ensure CallContext.Current.WithDuplicateContext clears itself after completion.\n\nThe release includes updates to dependencies, with log4net upgraded to version 2.0.17, and unused dependencies such as Microsoft.SourceLink.Bitbucket.Git, System.Net.Http, System.Threading.Tasks.Parallel, and System.ValueTuple removed to streamline the package.\n\nThese updates collectively enhance the package’s performance, reduce potential memory issues, and align the API with current standards for context and dependency management.",
